<title>POLAND: Polish August currency reserves fall to $21.93 bln.</title>
<headline>Polish August currency reserves fall to $21.93 bln.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-09-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish net foreign currency reserves, those held by the entire banking system, fell by $35 million in August to $21.925 billion and were $4.53 billion higher than a year ago, the National Bank of Poland said.</p>
<p>It said net reserves grew $1.49 billion in the January-August period compared to a $6.11 billion rise in the corresponding period of last year.</p>
</text>
